  "summary": "Redwood City Police Department announced it will review its Flock ALPR program ahead of its September 2026 contract renewal, citing recent revelations of unauthorized outside-agency access in neighboring Menlo Park and Mountain View. RCPD says it has found no evidence of unauthorized access to its 25 cameras, which logged 367 searches in 30 days, and will seek input from its Police Advisory Committee before reconfirming vendors.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Redwood City police are reviewing their use of automated license plate readers after other neighboring departments in Menlo Park and Mountain View acknowledged that outside agencies had unauthorized access to their systems.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Redwood City's contract with Flock expires in September 2026. This timing, the RCPD stated in the Feb. 13 press release, \"uniquely positions the city\" to gather feedback from the Police Advisory Committee and other stakeholders before reconfirming vendors and technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
